  data: {
    LLM: "In Phase 1, try to avoid cards that have many smaller cards of the same suit on the table. You want a small, manageable hand for the trick phase.\n\nThe 'Club Shield': Since Clubs cannot be trumped by Diamonds, they are the safest cards to lead if you want to ensure a trick follows standard suit-ranking without interference.\n\nPhase 1 Memory: Since you see every card entering the table/hands, remember who picked up the high Diamonds. Use your Clubs to neutralize their trump advantage during the second phase.",
    Player: "In Phase 1, try to avoid cards that have many smaller cards of the same suit on the table. You want a small, manageable hand for the trick phase.\n\nThe 'Club Shield': Since Clubs cannot be trumped by Diamonds, they are the safest cards to lead if you want to ensure a trick follows standard suit-ranking without interference.\n\nPhase 1 Memory: Since you see every card entering the table/hands, remember who picked up the high Diamonds. Use your Clubs to neutralize their trump advantage during the second phase.",
